{"format":1,"key":"zone:silverpine","path":"/lore/zone/silverpine","name":"Silverpine Forest","kind":"zone","label":"Zone","zone":{"key":"silverpine","name":"Silverpine Forest","path":"/lore/zone/silverpine"},"levels":"Levels 10-20","description":"Silverpine Forest is an eerie, mist-laden woodland stretching along Lordaeron's western coast between Tirisfal Glades and the sealed Greymane Wall.…","intro":[],"clips":[{"id":"zone:silverpine","part":"narration","anchor":"story","title":"The story","paras":["Silverpine Forest is an eerie, mist-laden woodland stretching along Lordaeron's western coast between Tirisfal Glades and the sealed Greymane Wall. Haunted by the lingering scars of the Scourge plague, it serves as the contested southern frontier of the Forsaken. Travelers here face feral worgen roaming the shadows, diseased gnolls, and hostile human enclaves.","Once celebrated as a lush wonder of Lordaeron through which noble travelers journeyed to Capital City, Silverpine Forest has withered under the touch of the Third War. Ghostly fogs weave between dying, silver-barked pines, and ruined farmsteads sit abandoned to the wilderness. To the north lies Tirisfal Glades, while the eastern shore borders Lordamere Lake. To the south stands the imposing and shut Greymane Wall, sealing off the isolationist kingdom of Gilneas from the surrounding chaos. The Forsaken maintain their central outpost at the Sepulcher, striving to secure the woods from enemies on all sides."],"hash":"28b3a0","voices":{"female-narrator":{"sha":"46460c90af","sec":62}}}],"sources":[{"kind":"wiki","title":"Silverpine Forest (Classic)","url":"https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Silverpine_Forest_(Classic)"},{"kind":"wiki","title":"Silverpine Forest","url":"https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Silverpine_Forest"}],"related":[{"p":"/lore/zone/shadowfang","n":"Shadowfang Keep","k":"dungeon"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/sepulcher","n":"Sepulcher","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/pyrewood-village","n":"Pyrewood Village","k":